# LEARNER C, LOCAL, TOWN05 + TOWN01, THE ACCUMULATED FIXES (user 2026-11-14: "Queue online train for best
# fixes with SAC with expert pinned rows"; "finetune locally first - try two towns and lets see before
# dedicating resources"; rule 2026-11-14: a fix stays on in every later run unless stated otherwise).
# = slurm/local_frl_c0emb_t01_ar2_xp.env (plain SAC; 10-head LayerNorm critic on a critic-trained 50-d
#   compression; expert rows PINNED in the main replay, never overwritten; the temperature tuned on the
#   RL's own rows only) with:
#   1. ENV_TOWNS=Town05,Town01: one Epic server and one env per town, both stepped at once (FRL_PARALLEL=1,
#      the loop of the 4-town cluster run: one update per transition, as with one town);
#   2. GOAL_ARRIVAL_MAX_SPEED=10: arrival counts only at <= 10 km/h, the 1.25M baseline's rule (user
#      2026-11-13); scored with slurm/il_eval_val_chw_jr_strict1m_ar8.env;
#   3. ACTION_REPEAT=8: one decision per 0.8 s (user 2026-11-14: "ok use action repeat at 8");
#   4. FRL_CONTROL: the pretrained CONTROL STREAM as the frozen trunk in place of c0's -- two frames 8 ticks
#      apart -> small CNN -> GRU that also takes the speed, pretrained at this decision rate by cloning the
#      expert with a lane head. CORRECTED 2026-11-14, after the run: this stream does NOT carry heading.
#      The "0.66-0.81" it was launched on was a probe fitted and scored on the same rows; on 123 episodes
#      it never loaded its own lane head gives offset R^2 0.38 and heading 0.10 (probe with episodes held
#      out: 0.40 / 0.08; scripts/control_stream_heldout.py). On the same episodes c0's GRU state probes
#      at 0.04 / 0.03, so heading is in neither (scripts/control_stream_vs_c0.py). DEBiT's
#      binocular goal features are unchanged. Pretraining also paired each frame with the speed one tick
#      later than the row carries online (GRU state moved by 2.2% of its sd: small).
#   RESULT OF THE ONE-TOWN RUN OF THIS CONFIGURATION (slurm/local_frl_control_t01_ar8.env, 2026-11-14):
#   training goal success 0.02 at 12,000 decisions; the 10k checkpoint scores 0/80 under the strict rule;
#   the IQL-warmed actor alone, before any SAC update, scores 2/80 (it comes within 1 m of the goal in
#   32 of 80 episodes but at 12-15 km/h, and drives about 30-40 m between faults). Do not relaunch as is.
#   5. FRL_EXPERT: M1 expert-driven episodes of Town01 + Town05 minus the probe hold-out, 342 + 322 episodes
#      (the 11-10 replay was built when only 160 Town01 shards were on this machine: 142 + 322), rebuilt through
#      that trunk at k=8 by scripts/build_expert_replay.py --control: action = the EXECUTED action at the
#      decision's first tick, rewards relabelled to this run's reward, the no_arrival cut -- 133,874 rows
#      (67,833 + 66,041), every tick the first tick of one decision (8 phases);
#   6. FRL_IQL_PRETRAIN=30000: IQL with FastRLAP's rules on those rows, on this learner's own critic and
#      actor, before the first online step (user 2026-11-14: "also pretrain critic with IQL first");
#   lane-centre shaping stays off (torch_rl.frl.carla.frl_refusals refuses it on; user 2026-11-14).
# KNOWN APPROXIMATION of item 5 at k=8: the expert changed its action every tick, so a row pairs the first
# tick's action with what the expert's own eight actions led to, not with holding that action for 0.8 s.
# FRL_* step counts are DECISIONS (8 ticks each): 60,000 decisions = 480,000 simulator ticks.
# A launcher may shorten the run (smoke test) by exporting these before the overlay is sourced:
_frl_steps=${FRL_MAX_STEPS:-60000}; _frl_ckpt=${FRL_CKPT_EVERY:-10000}; _frl_replay=${FRL_REPLAY:-60000}
. "$REPO/slurm/local_frl_c0emb_t01_ar2_xp.env"
export ENV_TOWNS=Town05,Town01
export FRL_PARALLEL=1
export ACTION_REPEAT=8
export GOAL_ARRIVAL_MAX_SPEED=10
export FRL_CONTROL=${FRL_CONTROL:-/home/robotlab/carla-sac-local/checkpoints/control_pre_n2_k8/step_6000}
export FRL_EXPERT=/home/robotlab/carla-sac-local/checkpoints/expert_replay/ctrl8_m1_t01t05_k8.npz
export FRL_IQL_PRETRAIN=${FRL_IQL_PRETRAIN:-30000}
export FRL_MAX_STEPS=$_frl_steps FRL_CKPT_EVERY=$_frl_ckpt
export FRL_REPLAY=$_frl_replay FRL_REPLAY_DEVICE=${FRL_REPLAY_DEVICE:-cpu}
